{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each time a bar of soap is used, its volume decreases by 10%. What is the minimum number of times\na new bar would have to be used so that less than one-half its volume remains?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c546ed5f60b14548fdd6b75885ffb093a0a17af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> uses, the volume of the soap is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb1be23a36c7994fe2eeef422ac47745d9f05640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0.9)^x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> So, we are trying to solve\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c8e65fde8d465714da2701fccbd1559c335567.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(0.9)^x &lt; 0.5.\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />\nWe can see that the solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805fcc0b07659abbcff2797b4d1176641f2f167d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c30566eb8cdc9bedece6cf3fe5e9f72d50b979e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(C)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a 